def elevator_floor(start_floor, commands, min_floor, max_floor):
    '''
    @param start_floor: an integer between min_floor and max_floor inclusive
    @param commands: a list of strings meaning the following: "UP" moves the elevator one floor up unless it is at max_floor; "DOWN" moves it one floor down unless it is at min_floor; any other string leaves the floor unchanged.
    @param min_floor: the lowest level the elevator can reach
    @param max_floor: the highest level the elevator can reach

    @return: the floor reached after applying every command to the start_floor
    '''
    floor = start_floor
    for command in commands:
        if command == 'UP':
            floor = min(floor + 1, max_floor)
        elif command == 'DOWN':
            floor = max(floor - 1, min_floor)
    return floor
```

Each command is examined in sequence. If the command is the string meaning up, the floor is raised by one, but not above the maximum allowed level. If the command is the string meaning down, the floor is lowered by one, but not below the minimum. Any other command has no effect.

