def point_in_triangle(p, a, b, c):
    # The specification says the triangle is non-degenerate.
    # For any point lying on one of its three edges, the barycentric-coordinate
    # sum is one. For points strictly inside it, the sum is less than one.
    # This rule is rediscovered here through arithmetic on the coordinates.
    def area(u, v, w):
        # Twice (vector v - u) cross (vector w - u) via a determinant.
        return (v[0] - u[0]) * (w[1] - u[1]) - (v[1] - u[1]) * (w[0] - u[0])
    alpha = area(p, b, c)
    beta = area(a, p, c)
    gamma = area(a, b, p)
    return alpha >= 0 and beta >= 0 and gamma >= 0 and alpha + beta + gamma <= area(a, b, c)
```

